  "help_title_1": "Get the blastQR app on other devices",
  "help_message_1_1": "Download the blastQR app on any device where you want to receive or send files. Both devices need to have the blastQR app.",
  "help_message_1_2": "Scan this QR code to download blastQR on another device. This particular code can be scanned using any regular QR code scanning app. blastQR is available for Android, iOS, Linux, macOS and Windows.",
  "help_title_2": "Sending a file",
  "help_message_2": "From the app's main screen, select the file or picture that you want to send.\n\nThe file will be encoded into a sequence of QR codes that you can then scan from another device that has blastQR installed.",
  "help_title_3": "Receiving a file",
  "help_message_3": "On another device, scan the QR code sequence using the blastQR app by selecting the 'Receive' tab.\n\nThe files you receive are stored in the 'Received' tab within the app.\n\nTIP: If the scanning process suddenly stops tap on the screen to resume.",
  "help_title_4": "Additional information",
  "help_message_4": "- blastQR file transfers work completely offline.\n\n- The transferred information is NOT encrypted and can be read by anyone who gains access to the QR code sequence unless using the 'Send password-encrypted' feature. Avoid using blastQR for transmitting any sensitive information without enabling encryption first and always use strong passwords.\n\n- Due to the nature of the technology, blastQR file transfers are not very fast by default. However, showing multiple codes at once (full-screen button) and raising the 'Playback speed' in Settings can increase the speed dramatically.\n\n- You can also use blastQR to scan regular QR codes.\n\n- blastQR is an open source project. You can find the source code at:",
